      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__sstep__api_1gabf6e86e82e3fec2d39be668525125a89" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int sstep_selftest</definition>
        <argsstring>(struct sstep *drv, uint32_t i_test_ma)</argsstring>
        <name>sstep_selftest</name>
        <param>
          <type>struct <ref refid="structsstep" kindref="compound">sstep</ref> *</type>
          <declname>drv</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>i_test_ma</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Test the power stage and the motor wiring before the first enable. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The outputs are switched on; for each phase in turn the fast loop raises the voltage slowly until the phase current reaches i_test_ma, holds it and lets it decay. It checks that no current flows with every leg low, that each phase reaches the current with the expected sign at a plausible duty cycle, and that the other phase stays below half of it. A rotor still moving into a step induces currents that break these conditions for a while: the hold and the decay go on until they have held for 2 ms and 5 ms in a row, for at most 100 ms each. Takes about 40 to 55 ms of fast loop periods (at most about 440 ms), then the outputs go off, ::SSTEP_EVENT_SELFTEST_DONE is reported by <ref refid="group__sstep__api_1gab80d582d293872a78abc1a1a35e8e8ef" kindref="member">sstep_slow_loop()</ref> and the result is in the status. A failure raises <ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1ga8f3bba3b4b2262a9d1bfc6df2b0ba2f1" kindref="member">SSTEP_FAULT_SELFTEST</ref>. The rotor moves to the nearest full step of the tested phase (at most one full step) and must be free to: an external torque that turns it fails the test. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>drv</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Driver instance. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>i_test_ma</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Test current [mA], 1 .. i_run_ma; typically 30 % of the rated current. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1gad80c1718aa6b968cfd521404803da291" kindref="member">SSTEP_OK</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The test runs. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1gaff8dbc7cce3d2e6d453df3c6d9ab1d14" kindref="member">SSTEP_ERR_PARAM</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>NULL pointer or i_test_ma out of range. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1ga145c9925476a6618b7d317935623ef33" kindref="member">SSTEP_ERR_STATE</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Not disabled, faulted, or a test is running. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1gad93b8d75937e0aba07a27ad33c058760" kindref="member">SSTEP_ERR_VBUS</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>No bus voltage sample yet, or outside the trip limits. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="group__sstep__defs_1ga80beeffdc48a72869fd2e6aa6bb84d32" kindref="member">SSTEP_ERR_UNSUPPORTED</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
